# gaming-presence — establishment RATE, not steady-state capacity
#
# Every connection-oriented shape here measures how many connections a broker
# HOLDS. None measures how fast it can ACCEPT them, and those are different
# limits: holding is memory, accepting is CPU, TLS, admission control and the
# accept queue.
#
# A game backend at session start is the shape that cares: tens of thousands of
# players connecting within seconds of a match opening. Same population as
# smart-home so the two are directly comparable — only the ramp changes, by 4x.
# If the hold cost is flat but the accept rate is not, that is the finding.
LANES=C
LANE_C_CONNS=50000
LANE_C_RAMP=10000
LANE_C_HOLD=60
